{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788419966-flZ4ZEUcnmwkkkhi5wGo","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nAll tasks have been completed successfully. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. BestOfN Module (`dspy/predict/best_of_n.py`)\n- Added `fail_count` parameter to control failure tolerance\n- Default behavior: raises only when all N attempts fail (default = N-1)\n- Clear error messages showing attempt number and temperature\n- Updated docstring with documentation\n\n### 2. Refine Module (`dspy/predict/refine.py`)\n- Fixed `fail_count` parameter handling for consistent behavior with BestOfN\n- Default behavior: raises only when all N attempts fail (default = N-1)\n- Updated docstring with documentation\n\n### 3. Documentation Created\n\n#### API Reference\n- **`docs/docs/api/modules/BestOfN.md`** - Comprehensive API documentation with:\n  - How the module works\n  - Parameter details with examples\n  - Error handling guidance\n  - Usage examples (basic, fail_count, threshold, use cases)\n  - Comparison with Refine\n  - Migration guide from assertion-based approaches\n\n- **`docs/docs/api/modules/Refine.md`** - Comprehensive API documentation with:\n  - How the module works with feedback mechanism\n  - Parameter details\n  - Error handling guidance\n  - Usage examples\n  - When to choose Refine vs BestOfN\n  - Best practices\n\n#### Tutorials\n- **`docs/docs/tutorials/output_refinement/index.md`** - Complete tutorial covering:\n  - Why output refinement matters\n  - BestOfN and Refine fundamentals\n  - 7 practical tutorials (basic usage, fail_count, early exit, factual correctness, response length, feedback, choosing the right tool)\n  - Real-world customer support example\n  - Comparison tables\n  - Migration guide\n\n### 4. Navigation Updated (`docs/mkdocs.yml`)\n- Added BestOfN and Refine to API Reference → Modules\n- Added \"Output Refinement\" tutorial to Tutorials section\n\n##